---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Affiliate Disclosure — CalcTax"
  description="How CalcTax earns revenue through affiliate partnerships while keeping all calculators free."
>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-14"><div class="prose">
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-3">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <p>
      CalcTax.ca is a free tax calculator website. To keep our tools free, we
      earn revenue through referral and affiliate links.
    </p>

    <h2>What This Means</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on this Site are affiliate or referral links. When you click one
      and sign up for a product or service, the company may pay us a commission
      or referral bonus. <strong>This comes at no extra cost to you</strong> — the price
      you pay is the same whether you use our link or go directly to the site.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Choose What to Recommend</h2>
    <p>
      We only recommend products we believe are genuinely useful for Canadians
      filing their taxes. Our recommendations are based on product quality,
      relevance to the calculator you're using, and value to the user — not on
      which company pays the highest commission.
    </p>
    <p>
      Affiliate partnerships <strong>never influence calculator results</strong>.
      Your tax calculations are based solely on CRA-published rates and the
      information you provide.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Current Partners</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Wealthsimple</strong> — Tax filing software and investment accounts. Our link is a personal referral link: if you sign up through it and fund an eligible Wealthsimple account, Wealthsimple may pay a bonus to both of us. Filing a tax return on its own doesn't earn us anything.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to Identify Affiliate Links</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate and referral links on this Site appear in boxes after your
      calculator results and in articles, each labelled with a short note saying
      it's a referral or affiliate link. All affiliate links open in a new tab
      and are tagged with <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the page source.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about our affiliate relationships, contact us at
      <a href="/contact">our contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
